--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.equal
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.Equal
type: REG_SZ, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list meaning any of
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: program, kernel, shared, none
applies: live — at the next generation

What stands at this machine's end of the flow.

A `program` is a socket some process owns; `kernel` is the stack itself
(resets, ICMP errors, neighbour discovery, tunnel outers); `shared` is
inbound multicast or broadcast delivered to every bound socket; `none`
means nothing listens and the stack will refuse it.

Only a `program` has the `Local.*` facts, so `Local.User.Present = 0` is
how you say "no program stands here".

The `Flow` layer only, and always present there.

--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.present
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.Present
type: REG_DWORD, or a decimal string
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: 1 the fact exists, 0 it does not
applies: live — at the next generation

What stands at this machine's end of the flow.

A `program` is a socket some process owns; `kernel` is the stack itself
(resets, ICMP errors, neighbour discovery, tunnel outers); `shared` is
inbound multicast or broadcast delivered to every bound socket; `none`
means nothing listens and the stack will refuse it.

Only a `program` has the `Local.*` facts, so `Local.User.Present = 0` is
how you say "no program stands here".

The `Flow` layer only, and always present there.

--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.user.<op>
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.User.<op>
type: REG_SZ, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list meaning any of
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: Equal, Present; a SID, or a well-known name
applies: live — at the next generation

Who owns the socket at this end.

Values: a SID (`S-1-5-19`), or a well-known name (`SYSTEM`,
`LocalService`, `NetworkService`, `Everyone`, `Administrators`, `Users`,
...).

Present on a `Flow` judgment when `Local` is `program`.

A name is turned into a SID exactly as the token was minted, so the rule
matches the token rather than a string; a misspelt name refuses the
generation rather than quietly matching nothing.

--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.group.<op>
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.Group.<op>
type: REG_SZ, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list meaning any of
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: Equal, Present; SIDs or well-known names
applies: live — at the next generation

The groups on the token at this end -- matches if any is present.

Deny-only groups are invisible here; the logon SID is among them.

Present on a `Flow` judgment when `Local` is `program`.

--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.integrity.<op>
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.Integrity.<op>
type: REG_DWORD, REG_QWORD, a decimal string, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: Equal, GreaterThan, LessThan, Present; a level, or a level name
applies: live — at the next generation

The integrity level of the token at this end.

Values: a level, or `untrusted`, `low`, `medium`, `high`, `system`.

Present on a `Flow` judgment when `Local` is `program`.

--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.confinement.<op>
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.Confinement.<op>
type: REG_SZ, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list meaning any of
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: Equal, Present; the confinement SID
applies: live — at the next generation

The confinement the program at this end runs under.

Present on a `Flow` judgment when the program is confined.

--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.capability.<op>
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.Capability.<op>
type: REG_SZ, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list meaning any of
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: Equal, Present; capability SIDs
