--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.service.<op>
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.Service.<op>
type: REG_SZ, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list meaning any of
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: Equal, Present; a service name, or its SID
applies: live — at the next generation

Which service the program at this end is.

Values: a service name (`resolvd`), or its `S-1-5-80-...` SID.

The name is resolved to the service's SID the same way the service's own
token was minted, so this matches the service and not a string.

Present on a `Flow` judgment when the program is a service.

--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> local.process.<op>
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Local.Process.<op>
type: REG_SZ, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list meaning any of
