valid: Equal, Present; a process GUID
applies: live — at the next generation

Which process holds the socket at this end.

Values: a process GUID, `8-4-4-4-12` hex (case-insensitive).

Present on a `Flow` judgment when `Local` is `program`.

--- machine\system\network\rules\<layer>\<rule...> remote.equal
canonical: Machine\System\Network\Rules\<Layer>\<rule...> Remote.Equal
type: REG_SZ, or a REG_MULTI_SZ list meaning any of
default: (absent — the rule does not condition on this fact)
valid: program, kernel, shared, none
applies: live — at the next generation

What stands at the other end, when that is also this machine.

The mirror of `Local`, and it exists only on loopback flows -- a peer on
another machine has no identity this kernel can know.

The `Remote.*` facts follow `Local.*` exactly, under the same
conditions.

